/target

# Rust build lockfile — this crate is a library, so we do not commit
# the crate-root Cargo.lock. The pattern is anchored to the crate root
# on purpose: fuzz/ is a *binary* crate whose Cargo.lock IS committed,
# and an unanchored `Cargo.lock` line would leave that file both
# tracked and ignored, which release-plz rejects as "uncommitted
# changes". See https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#why-do-binaries-have-cargolock-in-version-control-but-not-libraries
/Cargo.lock
